From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kraibse <33869366+kraibse@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 02:00:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] shader: route untracked 32-bit global atomics to their
 storage buffer

Every SPIR-V global atomic threw "SPIR-V Instruction is not
implemented", so a compute program whose atomic address the storage
buffer pass could not track failed to build and its dispatches were
dropped (four Ocarina compute pipelines; the dumps show U32 ADD/MAX,
S32 MIN and F32 ADD reductions).

Each 32-bit global atomic the program uses now gets a function on the
routing global loads and stores already use: the address picks the
candidate storage buffer, and the operation runs on its word. INC, DEC
and F32 add go through the storage buffer CAS loops. 64-bit and packed
forms still throw.

The test emits each of the 12 operations untracked; the modules pass
spirv-val (Vulkan 1.1, standard uniform buffer layout).

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (traced the pipeline failures, wrote the routing and test)
(cherry picked from commit 6b934346d76cf5a6753c9279df22f9df830fade4)
